  "evidence": "The registered descriptors identify the five pages and their create/destroy slots. Pressure explanation dispatches to two layout builders for page argument 2. Heart-rate explanation case 7 displays wear instructions; cases 3/4/5 use a text loop. Abnormal and resting heart rate build charts and register chart or information event callbacks. The settings catalog create/destroy functions are shared with a separate candidate descriptor, so event internals are not attributed exclusively to this descriptor.",
  "scope": "Recorded display and registration calls; no sensor, measurement algorithm or stored result hooks. The info callback may also be used by other heart-rate pages and is not separately named here.",
  "limitations": "Altering status text can misrepresent health data. Changing event callback registrations can break navigation and chart drawing. Values and image/text resources must remain valid. State slots are not thread barriers. Device behavior and recovery have not been validated.",
